Business Problem:
A company is having issues with accurately tracking employees hours worked. Employees clock in outside their scheduled shift windows, sometimes submit overlapping or duplicate clock-ins for the same shift, and there is no reliable way to catch these issues before they affect payroll. 


Why does it Matters?:
Inaccurate clock-ins lead to inaccurate time captures
Duplicate clock-in issues (Clocking in twice for the same shift)
Weak record of time actually worked

Scope:
Submit one clock in request; check if employee is currently employed; check if employee is scheduled for current time and date; reject clock-in if employee is not currently employed or not scheduled;  flag any clock-ins that are too early or too late relative to the scheduled shift; prevent duplicate or overlapping clock-ins; assign a unique request ID, timestamp, and status, to clock-in request; show employee a confirmation; keep record of clock-request ID

Out of Scope:
Clocking out or calculating total shift/hours worked; payroll calculations; scheduling shifts; PTO or time-off requests; tracking breaks; overtime calculation
